  {
    "id": "3d1a45c7f74c9316b143",
    "source": "Whether the party NOTICES something they are not actively searching for (a trap, a hidden door, an ambusher lying in wait, a lie in an NPC's words) is decided by passive scores, not a roll. Before you reveal or hide such a thing, call check_notice with how hard it is to spot and which sense applies (perception, insight, or investigation); the server compares every character's passive score and tells you who notices. Narrate only what the noticing characters could know. Never simply declare that the party does or does not spot a hidden thing without this call. When a creature is what hides (or lies, for insight), pass againstEnemyId in a fight or againstMonster (its stat block by name) out of one instead of a difficulty: the server rolls its Stealth (or Deception) and uses that as the DC. Off the battle map the server reads the light from the location (underground is dark, a building is lit, the open air follows the hour) and from the party's torches and lanterns; pass light when you know better. A blinded character automatically fails a check that needs sight, a deafened one a check that needs hearing: give request_roll a reason that names what they are trying to perceive.",
    "sourceHash": "3d1a45c7f74c9316b143060ef5f8856a1a0dd89fb69bff88314c27587c66ddef",
    "kinds": [
      "display-property"
    ],
    "sites": [
      {
        "file": "src/lib/dm/prompt-rules.ts",
        "line": 137
      }
    ]
  },
